==English==
{{Wikipedia|sherd, shard, potsherd}}
===Etymology===

''Sherd'' and ''shard'' come from the Old English word ''[[sceard]]''.

===Alternative spellings===
*[[sherd]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

#A [[piece]] of [[broken]] [[glass]] or [[pottery]], especially one found in an [[archaeological]] [[dig]]
#A tough [[scale]], [[sheath]], or [[shell]]; it is especially used as a term to refer to the [[elytra]] of a beetle.
#An instance of game world in a [[MMOG]], usually used to refer to the game world within a specific game server. (From ''[[w:Ultima Online|Ultima Online]]'')

